{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwyA9BUVd8tCVFU7BAp6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. Vitest 5.0 added `vi.when`, which works much like jest-when. The installed Vitest 5.0.3 includes it, and I confirmed that in its type definitions (`node_modules/vitest/dist/index.d.ts`). You pass it a spy and set what each set of arguments should return, for example `vi.when(spy).calledWith(1).thenReturn(0)`, or `.thenResolve(...)` for promises. If a call should fail when no arguments match, use `vi.when(spy, { onUnmatched: 'throw' })`. It also supports `using w = vi.when(spy)`, which scopes the behaviors to that block. On Vitest versions before 5, you'd still need the `jest-when` package or a `mockImplementation` that checks the arguments itself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":743,"cache_read_input_tokens":28166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":743},"output_tokens":262,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d323a7ac-4dcc-4e20-84b3-86466f07797b","uuid":"ef4ac22f-3ffb-443f-9674-0348446f4a86","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:44:00.447Z","request_id":"req_011CfwyA8GuNR6f6vE2Yzazq"}
